    {
     "token": "origin",
     "text": "Standing at Vector.ZERO,\n\nPoint zero, * ,\nVector(0,0,0)\nThe root of all vectors.\n\nThe origin, No turning back.",
     "by": "hand",
     "place": "foyer",
     "lock": [
      0,
      0
     ],
     "placed_by": "grid",
     "claimed": true,
     "note": "A corner, not a cell. Four cells meet here and none of them contains it, which is why nothing could be centred on the origin until the basin was made even: an odd one has a middle cell, and a corner is not a cell. Three of its four quadrants lie in coordinates no map row can name — the building can stand there, the language cannot. So it was not placed but excavated, two metres down under glass, and became visible by subtraction. While it was being dug, five systems walked into it: a bench, a column, a cornice, a joint, a lit strip. To each of them this was cell (0,0), ordinary floor. It is only the origin because someone says so.",
